# Production MCP is api/mcp.py + commons_mcp.py and their import graph.
# The Git-backed board corpus is read over HTTPS, not from this bundle.
# Hobby upload cap is 5000 files (api-upload-free). Deny root entries, then
# allow only the runtime graph. A denylist of p/chunks still left 9k+ files
# (muhl, projection, infra, ground, host) and production deploy failed.
# Bare * and root /* both failed on Vercel CLI 56.1.0: nested un-ignores
# never applied (runs 33218271833 and 33219467177 uploaded 7 root files,
# api/mcp.py missing). Production deploy stages the runtime graph instead
# and does not copy this file into that directory. Keep the allowlist as
# the local/root-deploy contract and the bound git-matcher test.
/*
!api/
!api/**
!carriers/
!carriers/**
!integrations/
!integrations/grokcom_revenue/
!integrations/grokcom_revenue/**
!protocol/
!protocol/**
!host/
host/*
!host/observatory.py
!host/owner_context.py
!commons_mcp.py
!commons_mcp_app.html
!model_language.py
!relay_manifest.py
!owner_enroll.py
!owner_net.py
!vercel.json
# Named corpus denies stay explicit so the bound test keeps reading them.
p
chunks
posts.json
